        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat: support loopback-only LM Studio vision classification",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds OpenAI-compatible local vision classification for LM Studio while keeping\nthe existing Ollama path as the default.\n\n- Select with `--local-model-api openai`; base URLs such as\n  `http://127.0.0.1:1234/v1` normalize to the chat-completions endpoint.\n- Require every endpoint hostname resolution to be loopback-only. Revalidate\n  redirects and DNS again at dial time; bypass ambient HTTP proxies.\n- Persist the requested endpoint, every endpoint that actually responded, HTTP\n  request/response counts, loopback scope, and transmitted-image provenance.\n- Mark non-image rows terminal for vision classification while leaving remote\n  images retryable.\n- Prioritize new pending rows before retryable metadata-classified rows.\n\n`export` is intentionally not part of this PR. It needs a separate product\nproposal and real Apple Photos proof.\n\n## Verification\n\nExact head: `7a119845935e73801a919314c68837b7703601f9`\n\nFull local gate:\n\n```sh\nGOWORK=off go mod verify\nGOWORK=off go mod tidy -diff\nGOWORK=off go vet ./...\nGOWORK=off go run golang.org/x/tools/cmd/deadcode@v0.45.0 -test ./...\nGOWORK=off go test -count=1 ./...\nGOWORK=off go build -trimpath -o /private/tmp/photoscrawl-pr3 ./cmd/photoscrawl\n```\n\nResults: module verification clean; tidy diff empty; vet clean; deadcode empty;\nall packages passed; built binary SHA-256\n`aa0de3ab3c7434805df573c188752472a3a091e016e154907748d1b680598295`.\n\nReal-binary behavior proof used a synthetic SQLite archive and a loopback\nOpenAI-compatible HTTP stub:\n\n- Valid loopback redirect: one asset and three content observations, zero\n  failures. The CLI and SQLite model-run metadata recorded both responding\n  endpoints and two HTTP requests/two responses. Per-asset evidence recorded\n  the final endpoint and 24 transmitted fixture bytes.\n- Direct `192.0.2.10` endpoint: exit 1 with loopback-only rejection.\n- Loopback redirect to `192.0.2.10`: one terminal content failure; only the\n  loopback redirect endpoint appeared in provenance, with one request/response.\n  The stub's final-response count did not increase.\n- Remote-only video: first run stored `content_unavailable` with zero waiting;\n  second run processed zero rows and made no model request.\n- `photoscrawl export`: exit 2; top-level usage contains no export command.\n\nBehavior-validator contract: 6 pass, 0 fail, 0 blocked. Final AutoReview:\nclean, no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nHosted CI `CI/test` passed on the exact head:\nhttps://github.com/openclaw/photoscrawl/actions/runs/29556214804\n\nThanks @mbelinky for the original LM Studio/OpenAI-compatible classifier work.\n",
